-- title:
--   Extracting an n-th root of a branch coordinate
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation ring (a commutative domain, discretely valued, complete for its maximal-adic topology), let $\pi \in W$ be irreducible, and let $m, n$ be positive integers with $n$ invertible in $W$. Write $R_e := \mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2, W)/(X_0X_1 - C(\pi^e))$ for the crossing model `UVCrossingModel W (π ^ e)`, with distinguished elements `U (π ^ e)`, `V (π ^ e)` and with `const (π ^ e) w` the image of the constant series $C(w)$. Let $u$ be a unit of $R_{mn}$, let $K_0$ be a fraction field of $R_{mn}$, and let $F$ be a field which is an algebra over both $K_0$ and $R_{mn}$ compatibly, containing an element $\theta$ with $\theta^n$ equal to the image of $u \cdot U(\pi^{mn})$ in $F$, and such that the $K_0$-subfield of $F$ generated by $\theta$ is all of $F$. Then the integral closure $B$ of $R_{mn}$ in $F$ is a finite $R_{mn}$-module, $B$ is a local ring, and there is a ring isomorphism $e : B \xrightarrow{\sim} R_m$ such that $e$ carries the image of `const (π ^ (m * n)) w` to `const (π ^ m) w` for every $w \in W$; for some unit $v$ of $R_m$, $e^{-1}(v \cdot U(\pi^m))$ equals $\theta$ in $F$; and for some units $v_1, v_2$ of $R_m$, $e$ carries the images of $U(\pi^{mn})$ and $V(\pi^{mn})$ to $v_1 \cdot U(\pi^m)^n$ and $v_2 \cdot V(\pi^m)^n$ respectively.
--
--   This is the algebraic normalisation statement that adjoining an $n$-th root of a unit multiple of one branch coordinate of the node $xy = \pi^{mn}$, with $n$ invertible in $W$, produces exactly the node $UV = \pi^{m}$, the two branches being ramified of degree $n$. It is used in the construction of isomorphisms between completed local rings of crossing type along tame cyclic covers, namely by [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_uvCrossingModel_of_isGalois_of_isCyclic_of_isUnramifiedAt_of_residue`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_uvCrossingModel_of_isGalois_of_isCyclic_of_isUnramifiedAt_of_residue) and its root-of-unity variant.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_exists_ringEquiv_integralClosure_uvCrossingModel_pow_of_pow_eq_unit_mul_U.lean

